{"next clamps offset with Math.min(offset + limit, user_count) so when you hit the last page offset becomes user_count and the backend returns zero members and a blank page": 0.7206517457962036, "totalPages uses Math.floor(user_count/limit)+1, so when user_count is an exact multiple of limit we report an extra phantom page with no members": 0.8665292263031006, "alias_level from the flat payload is never assigned before group.save, so creating a group with a non-default alias_level from the UI silently drops that value": 0.6260987520217896, "members now always runs with limit=50/offset even for non-automatic groups but the public group/members template has no pagination controls, so the UI never loads past the first page": 0.9299448132514954}